# NestJS Testing Excellence

## Testing Layers

| Layer | Tool | Scope |
|-------|------|-------|
| Unit | Jest + `createTestingModule` | Single service/guard/pipe in isolation |
| Integration | Jest + `@nestjs/testing` | Full module with real DB or in-memory substitute |
| E2E | Jest + Supertest | HTTP request → response through the full app |

## Unit Testing Services

- Use `createTestingModule` to instantiate only the class under test
- Mock every dependency with `{ provide: Token, useValue: mockObject }`
- Reset mocks in `beforeEach` to prevent state leakage between tests

```typescript
// ✅ users.service.spec.ts
import { Test, TestingModule } from '@nestjs/testing'
import { getRepositoryToken } from '@nestjs/typeorm'
import { Repository } from 'typeorm'
import { ConflictException, NotFoundException } from '@nestjs/common'
import { UsersService } from './users.service'
import { User } from './entities/user.entity'

const mockUser: User = {
  id: 'uuid-1',
  email: 'alice@example.com',
  password: 'hashed',
  displayName: 'Alice',
}

describe('UsersService', () => {
  let service: UsersService
  let repo: jest.Mocked<Pick<Repository<User>, 'findOneBy' | 'find' | 'create' | 'save' | 'remove'>>

  beforeEach(async () => {
    repo = {
      findOneBy: jest.fn(),
      find: jest.fn(),
      create: jest.fn(),
      save: jest.fn(),
      remove: jest.fn(),
    }

    const module: TestingModule = await Test.createTestingModule({
      providers: [
        UsersService,
        { provide: getRepositoryToken(User), useValue: repo },
      ],
    }).compile()

    service = module.get(UsersService)
  })

  describe('create', () => {
    it('returns the saved user when email is unique', async () => {
      repo.findOneBy.mockResolvedValue(null)
      repo.create.mockReturnValue(mockUser)
      repo.save.mockResolvedValue(mockUser)

      const result = await service.create({ email: mockUser.email, password: '12345678' })

      expect(result).toEqual(mockUser)
      expect(repo.save).toHaveBeenCalledWith(mockUser)
    })

    it('throws ConflictException when email already exists', async () => {
      repo.findOneBy.mockResolvedValue(mockUser)

      await expect(
        service.create({ email: mockUser.email, password: '12345678' }),
      ).rejects.toThrow(ConflictException)
    })
  })

  describe('findOneOrFail', () => {
    it('returns the user when found', async () => {
      repo.findOneBy.mockResolvedValue(mockUser)
      await expect(service.findOneOrFail('uuid-1')).resolves.toEqual(mockUser)
    })

    it('throws NotFoundException when user does not exist', async () => {
      repo.findOneBy.mockResolvedValue(null)
      await expect(service.findOneOrFail('uuid-999')).rejects.toThrow(NotFoundException)
    })
  })
})
```

## Unit Testing Controllers

- Mock the service and assert that the controller calls the right service method with the right args
- Do not test HTTP status codes or headers in unit tests — that belongs in E2E tests

```typescript
// ✅ users.controller.spec.ts
import { Test } from '@nestjs/testing'
import { UsersController } from './users.controller'
import { UsersService } from './users.service'

describe('UsersController', () => {
  let controller: UsersController
  let service: jest.Mocked<UsersService>

  beforeEach(async () => {
    const module = await Test.createTestingModule({
      controllers: [UsersController],
      providers: [
        {
          provide: UsersService,
          useValue: {
            create: jest.fn(),
            findAll: jest.fn(),
            findOneOrFail: jest.fn(),
            update: jest.fn(),
            remove: jest.fn(),
          },
        },
      ],
    }).compile()

    controller = module.get(UsersController)
    service = module.get(UsersService) as jest.Mocked<UsersService>
  })

  it('delegates creation to the service', async () => {
    const dto = { email: 'alice@example.com', password: '12345678' }
    const created = { id: 'uuid-1', ...dto, displayName: null }
    service.create.mockResolvedValue(created as any)

    const result = await controller.create(dto)

    expect(service.create).toHaveBeenCalledWith(dto)
    expect(result).toEqual(created)
  })
})
```

## E2E Testing with Supertest

- Bootstrap the full `AppModule` once per suite using `beforeAll`; close the app in `afterAll`
- Use a dedicated test database (SQLite in-memory or a Docker container) to avoid polluting production data
- Seed and clear data in `beforeEach` so tests remain independent

```typescript
// ✅ test/users.e2e-spec.ts
import { Test, TestingModule } from '@nestjs/testing'
import { INestApplication, ValidationPipe, ClassSerializerInterceptor } from '@nestjs/common'
import { Reflector } from '@nestjs/core'
import * as request from 'supertest'
import { AppModule } from '../src/app.module'

describe('UsersController (e2e)', () => {
  let app: INestApplication

  beforeAll(async () => {
    const moduleFixture: TestingModule = await Test.createTestingModule({
      imports: [AppModule],
    }).compile()

    app = moduleFixture.createNestApplication()

    // Mirror the global setup from main.ts
    app.useGlobalPipes(
      new ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, transform: true }),
    )
    app.useGlobalInterceptors(
      new ClassSerializerInterceptor(app.get(Reflector)),
    )

    await app.init()
  })

  afterAll(async () => {
    await app.close()
  })

  it('POST /users → 201 with created user', async () => {
    const dto = { email: 'e2e@example.com', password: 'supersecret' }

    const { body, status } = await request(app.getHttpServer())
      .post('/users')
      .send(dto)

    expect(status).toBe(201)
    expect(body).toMatchObject({ email: dto.email })
    expect(body).not.toHaveProperty('password')  // @Exclude() on entity
  })

  it('POST /users → 409 on duplicate email', async () => {
    const dto = { email: 'e2e@example.com', password: 'supersecret' }

    await request(app.getHttpServer()).post('/users').send(dto)
    const { status } = await request(app.getHttpServer()).post('/users').send(dto)

    expect(status).toBe(409)
  })

  it('GET /users/:id → 404 for unknown id', async () => {
    const { status } = await request(app.getHttpServer())
      .get('/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000')

    expect(status).toBe(404)
  })
})
```

## Key Rules

- Always call `app.close()` in `afterAll` to prevent open handle warnings from Jest
- Mirror `main.ts` global pipes/interceptors inside the test bootstrap so validation behaves identically
- Prefer `jest.Mocked<SomeService>` over casting to `any` for proper type-checking in mocks
- Test service methods directly in unit tests and HTTP layer behavior (status codes, headers) in E2E tests — don't mix concerns
- Use `jest.config.ts` with separate projects for unit and E2E tests to control execution independently
